  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Determination\\n\\nThe integration should expect **`InvalidCursorError` from `@ordarium/core`, with `error.code === \\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"`** — a dedicated, fail-closed cursor rejection. It should *not* expect a generic ledger failure (`LedgerCorruptError` / `LEDGER_CORRUPT`), nor a silent restart from the beginning of the feed, nor a capability error.\\n\\nMessage: `\\\"The change cursor is not a valid durable position; refusing to guess a resume point\\\"`.\\n\\n## Evidence chain (local, in-workspace)\\n\\n1. **The only local text that mentions cursor rejection is a self-voided legacy register.** `docs/engineering/10-legacy-error-codes.md` is three lines long and says the *1.2.0 line* reported \\\"a generic ledger failure rather than a dedicated cursor-rejection error,\\\" with status **\\\"superseded — void for the current pinned line.\\\"** So on its face it describes the *opposite* of a dedicated error and explicitly disclaims applicability to the current line.\\n\\n2. **The current pinned line is Ordarium 1.3.1, not 1.2.0.** `package.json` pins `@ordarium/core`, `@ordarium/ledger-sqlite` and `@ordarium/host-kit` to `ordarium-v1.3.1` tarballs; the installed artifacts confirm `\\\"version\\\": \\\"1.3.1\\\"`",
